{{also|Lucifer|Lúcifer}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Originally a [[brand name]] for matches made by Samuel Jones from 1830, soon used [[generic]]ally for self-igniting matches of any brand. From {{m|la|lucifer||bringer of light}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|British|archaic}} A self-igniting [[match]], ie. one which could be [[light|lit]] by [[strike|striking]] on any [[surface]] (as opposed to [[safety match]]es which only light against the material on the side of the [[box]]).
#* '''1915''', {{w|George Asaf}}, song ''Pack up your Troubles''
#*: While you've a lucifer to light your fag,<br>Smile, boys, that's the style.

====Descendants====
